  "//": [
    "Known-ordinary hobby words, Danish and English (D2, DESIGN.md §5.2 (5)). An exact match of a tag's normalised text (normalizeTag().norm) turns a detector flag off, so nobody's 'madlavning' or 'board games' is treated as sensitive.",
    "How it was made: written by hand on 2026-11-04 by the scaffold's architect (an AI assistant) from everyday hobbies (reading, food and drink, outdoors, sport, games, crafts, music, culture, tech, animals), choosing only words that name an activity and say nothing about health, beliefs, sexuality, politics, ethnic origin or union membership. Hobby words next to those topics are left out on purpose (church choir, meditation, mindfulness, veganism, pride, named languages such as 'spanish', parenting). No user data was used.",
    "Checked in CI (test/knownOrdinary.test.ts): every entry is already normalised, 2–40 characters, unique, and has no Art. 9 lexicon hit, blocklist or PII match or third-party pattern. The lexicon is checked before this list, so a lexicon term can never be switched off here.",
    "Why it needs no maintenance: it can only make a tag ordinary for an exact everyday hobby word. A word that is missing falls back to the detector, and the user can still choose 'This isn't sensitive for me' for their own holding. Adding words is optional and never urgent; removing one only makes the app more cautious. Bump `version` on any change, because stored tags record it."
  ],
